  "description": "Probe of the categorical magic condition (shell-self-duality) on atom braids. For each (Z, N), tests whether x_λ(β) = x_{λ*}(β) for every partition pair (λ, λ*) ⊢ 3A in the Wedderburn decomposition of H_{3A}(q) at q_0. NO Vol_hyp, NO knot identification, NO census search. Purely algebraic. Predicts: Z=N atoms are categorically magic (all dual pairs); Z≠N atoms are non-magic (some pairs not dual).",
